---
print — Print values                                                         core · tier 0 · since 0.1.0 · 1.0 · exact

USAGE
    print(x, ...)

DESCRIPTION
    Prints each value through the display interface that `core` declares and every type implements, so a
    frame, a table, a number or a text prints the way it prints when a statement that is not a `let` stands
    on its own. Several values print one after another, each on its own lines.

    `print` returns nothing: it is a statement, and its result cannot be bound or passed on (Z0206).

ARGUMENTS
    x           Any. The value to print; any type.

VALUE
    Nothing.

WARNINGS AND NOTES
    Z0206   the result of print is bound or passed; it has none

ACCURACY
    Exact.

SEE ALSO
    describe, summary

EXAMPLES
    > print(42)
    42
    > print("hello", 0.1)
    hello
    0.1
